A minimalistic composition featuring three identical monks in saffron robes seated in a circular arrangement on a stark white void, each facing a different direction—one reaching upward with open palm, one with hands folded in stillness, one in a pose of perfect ambiguity with arms neither extended nor withdrawn. Soft shadows pool beneath them like spilled ink. The scene evokes paradox and philosophical humor through pure geometric simplicity, with negative space dominating the canvas. Muted earth tones against pristine emptiness, clean lines, meditative atmosphere with a subtle undercurrent of absurdist wit.
